<description>
Copy each red or teal marker upward from the blue row and connect it back with blue cells.

Input structure
- The background is the dominant empty color.
- All foreground pixels lie in one full-width horizontal row.
- That row is blue except for red and/or teal marker pixels.

Rule
- A red marker is copied four rows above itself; a teal marker is copied three rows above itself.
- Fill the intervening cells in the same column with blue, leaving the original row unchanged.

Key insight
- The marker color encodes the upward distance of the vertical stem.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "red and teal marker pixels embedded in the full-width blue row",
  "path": "vertical ray upward in the marker's column, four rows for red markers and three rows for teal markers",
  "trajectory": "copy the marker color at the top of the ray and paint the intervening cells blue",
  "transform": "leave the original row and all other background cells unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 9-13 rows x 6-11 cols, background black(0)
  blue_row:
    position: single full-width horizontal row of non-background cells
    composition: all cells are blue(1) except for marker pixels
    endpoints: first and last column are always blue [observed]
    row_index: must have >= 4 rows above (to fit tallest stem)
    rows_below: 1-5 [observed]
  markers:
    count: 1-4 per row
    colors: teal(8) => 3-row stem, red(2) => 4-row stem
    placement: interior columns only (not col 0 or last col) [observed]
  output_rule: |
    For each marker at (row, col) with color C and distance D:
      - Place C at (row - D, col)
      - Fill (row - D + 1) through (row - 1) in that column with blue(1)
      - Original blue row unchanged
    All other cells remain black.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims: rows in [9,13], cols in [6,11]
    2. Pick blue_row index R such that R >= 4 and R <= rows - 2
    3. Fill row R entirely with blue(1)
    4. Pick 1-4 marker columns from interior cols [1, cols-2]; place teal(8) or red(2) at each
    5. For each marker, build the vertical stem upward in the output (guaranteed to fit since R >= 4)
    6. Input = output with stems erased (only the blue row with markers remains)
```
</generation_spec>
